<p>UK health authorities said the number of meningitis cases under investigation in Kent has risen to 27, including 15 laboratory-confirmed cases, as they widened their response to an outbreak centered on the University of Kent and the Canterbury nightclub Club Chemistry. Two people have died: a 21-year-old University of Kent student and an 18-year-old schoolgirl from Faversham. Officials also broadened advice for Club Chemistry attendees, urging more people to come forward for antibiotics and vaccination. The focus now is on limiting further spread before students leave for the Easter vacation. The University of Kent has launched a targeted MenB vaccination program, and British officials said it was still too soon to know whether the outbreak had been contained.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/B26rkQ18guXMET6foSXIsYm2dBVxIpb6Inn-SK-hXJqITUJoTonY52tbKB5JnZM3PqPxPQwBGaZI2m6iaXr_G4ZKCs0j9FjWyvYUzVHCvNqc' alt='People queue to receive vaccinations at the Sports centre on the University of Kent campus, following an outbreak of meningitis cases in Kent, in Canterbury, Britain on March 18, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Age profile: UK health authorities said all those affected are young people, underscoring how heavily the outbreak has hit student-age groups.</li><li>School spread: UK health authorities confirmed cases involving students at four schools in Kent, as well as one student at a higher education institution in London.</li><li>Strain profile: Six of the nine confirmed cases cited earlier in the outbreak were identified as group B meningococcal disease, the strain targeted by the campus vaccination drive.</li><li>Rapid increase: Authorities said the number of cases under investigation rose from 15 on Tuesday to 27 by Thursday.</li></ul><blockquote>Anyone who attended Club Chemistry on March 5, 6, or 7, please come forward to receive antibiotics - Keir Starmer</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UK Health Security Agency: The agency said health teams were working to identify close contacts of people who became ill as the investigation widened. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983724/uk-meningitis-outbreak-cases-rise-to-27'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Prime Minister Keir Starmer: Starmer used Parliament to amplify the public appeal around Club Chemistry, signaling direct political support for the containment effort. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983724/uk-meningitis-outbreak-cases-rise-to-27'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Health Secretary Wes Streeting: Streeting said the eligibility window should cover anyone who attended Club Chemistry from March 5 to March 15, reflecting a broader precautionary approach than the initial appeal. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/mar/19/number-meningitis-cases-linked-kent-outbreak-rises'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/health/article/2026/03/19/uk-meningitis-outbreak-cases-rise-to-at-least-27_6751605_14.html'>UK meningitis outbreak cases rise to at least 27</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983724/uk-meningitis-outbreak-cases-rise-to-27'>UK meningitis outbreak cases rise to 27</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3347095/unprecedented-spread-uk-races-contain-deadly-meningitis-outbreak'>‘Unprecedented in spread’: UK races to contain deadly meningitis outbreak</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/18/world/europe/uk-meningitis-outbreak-kent-symptoms-vaccine.html'>As a Meningitis Outbreak Spreads in Kent, UK, Here’s What to Know</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/british-health-official-says-too-soon-to-declare-kent-meningitis-outbreak-contained'>British health official says too soon to declare Kent meningitis outbreak contained</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/mar/19/number-meningitis-cases-linked-kent-outbreak-rises'>Meningitis vaccine eligibility expanded after Kent outbreak rises to 27</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>